{Metaform_Schema} :=

METAFORM(
  id          := [metaform_id],
  description := [description of the AT and AUE present],

  elements := [

    # The core node: the project itself. An element with a name and the
    # namespace address core. It is not a type, so it takes no part in the
    # namespace and is never reversed or read as one. namespace carries
    # only a single placeholder word "core", Its job is
    # connective: everything the intake records connects to it — the
    # AUEs, the collections, and the CQUs. In a single-artifact project
    # it holds the one AUE directly.
    ELEMENT(
      namespace_address := core,
      name := [canonical name | project name | inferred name],

      elements := [

        # The AUE: the root of the project's elements.
        ELEMENT(
          namespace_address := [code|document|media|data dotted namespace address],
          name_length       := [proper_noun_lookback_segment_count],
          name              := [Canonical Name (Project official terminology)],
          role              := AUE,

          elements := [
            ELEMENT(
              namespace_address := [dotted namespace address],
              name_length       := [proper_noun_lookback_segment_count],
              name              := [Canonical Name (Project official terminology)],
              role              := [DE|SE|NE],
              joins             := []
            )
          ],

          joins := [JOIN(...)]
        ),

        # Each CQU: defined at downstream.cqu, beside the AUE.
        ELEMENT(
          namespace_address := downstream.cqu.[CQU type],
          name_length       := [proper_noun_lookback_segment_count],
          name              := [industry title of the CQU role],
          role              := CQU,
          elements          := [],

          joins := [
            JOIN(
              type    := purpose,
              purpose := [RE Operative Purpose],
              ef      := [PE Encounter Function within this RE encounter],
              ifd     := [send|receive|both],

              elements := [
                # The PE.
                ELEMENT(
                  namespace_address := [dotted namespace address],
                  name_length       := [proper_noun_lookback_segment_count],
                  name              := [Canonical Name (Project official terminology)],
                  role              := [DE|SE|NE],
                  elements          := [],

                  joins := [
                    # One level deeper: what this PE receives, in the same JOIN form, repeated at every depth.
                    JOIN(...)
                  ]
                )
              ]
            )
          ]
        )
      ],

      joins := []
    )
  ]
)

# Notes
+> The core node is an element with a name and the namespace address core; it is not a type, and it holds the AUEs, the collections, and the CQUs.
+> The element owning a purpose join is the RE; its nested element is the PE.
+> PE is not a role. An element may receive in one join and provide in another.
+> purpose is the only join type.
+> An annealed part is a join one level deeper, in the joins of the PE it is part of; it is not a separate top-level element.
+> An element is written in full where it first appears; where it appears again it carries namespace_address, name_length, name and role only.
+> Project elements remain under code|document|media|data regardless of join role.
+> upstream.* links external code|document|media|data that provide into the project.
+> downstream.cqu.* links external CQUs; other downstream.* entries link external receivers.
+> upstream/downstream are project-boundary links, not join-direction namespaces.
+> Links are not decomposed and hold no project elements beneath them.
+> An element's refs are items of the sources layer, not fields of the metaform.
+> Elements and joins nest in the same form at every depth. Trace as deep as the artifact's functionality goes; a part stops being traced on its own only where its parent's purpose carries it, never at the depth this template happens to show.
